{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929","id":"msg_016x5cQPUgeTA6zb2P6U2EeL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! All tasks completed successfully. Let me provide a summary of what was implemented:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully implemented vim-style navigation for the month view calendar. Here's what was accomplished:\n\n### Implemented Features:\n1. **h/l navigation** - Move left/right between days in the same week\n2. **j/k navigation** - Move up/down between weeks (7 days at a time)\n3. **w/e navigation** - Jump to start/end of the current week\n4. **b/f navigation** - Navigate to previous/next month while preserving day position\n5. **g command** - Opens a prompt to jump to a specific date (YYYY-MM-DD format)\n6. **G command** - Instantly jumps to today's date\n\n### Key Implementation Details:\n- Added `InputMode` enum to handle normal vs date-prompt mode\n- Created helper methods in `MonthView`: `move_to_week_start()`, `move_to_week_end()`, `move_to_prev_month()`, `move_to_next_month()`, `jump_to_today()`\n- Added input buffer for date prompt with visual feedback\n- Month navigation intelligently handles day overflow (e.g., Jan 31 → Feb 28)\n\n### Additional Fixes:\n- Enabled serde feature for chrono to support date serialization\n- Fixed UUID generation race condition by adding atomic counter\n\n### Quality Checks:\n✅ All 42 tests pass (`cargo test`)  \n✅ Clippy passes with only acceptable warnings  \n✅ Navigation feels vim-like and intuitive  \n\n<promise>COMPLETE</promise>"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":514,"cache_read_input_tokens":61604,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":514,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":380,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bbc448c1-77c9-466c-8d2a-f1bf7c18d2e5","uuid":"c97c8030-f7ab-4b58-88b4-477c9f1164e6"}
